<div name="tabstrip">
	<ul>
		<li name="query" class="k-state-active">Query</li>
		<li name="filters">Filters & Actions</li>
		<li name="preview">Preview</li>
	</ul>
	<div name="GBWizard" class="component tab-content" >
		<div class="container">			
			<ul class="fieldList">				
				<li>
					<label>Grid Name</label>
						<div class="value">
						<input type="text" name="gridname" />
					</div>
				</li>
				<li>
					<label>Filterable</label>
						<div class="value">
						<input type="checkbox" name="filterable" checked />
					</div>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<hr />
			<p> If you can do it in javascript you can do it here! ...Almost</p>
			<p> Inside your template you have access to all selected properties, if you keep you're code between the hashes like this --  #: {Code Here} # -- then you can use javascript </p>
			<p> e.g. to multiply your Id by 2 simply put #: Id * 2 # in the template </p>
			<p class="error">Reminder: remember to null check when doing complex equations </p>
			<p><a href="https://docs.telerik.com/kendo-ui/framework/templates/overview" target="_blank" >More info...</a></p>
